Software TSO at the forwarding balk sites ("Phase A").

Adds tcp_tso_chop(), the software TCP segmenter FreeBSD never had
as a callable function (the sfxge(4) arithmetic emitting mbuf
chains), and replaces the bare MTU balks in ip_tryforward(),
ip6_tryforward() and ip6_forward() with the ordered handler: fits
-> send; egress splits in hardware -> pass whole; CSUM_TSO ->
chop in software (clamped to the egress MTU) and send the chain;
else -> ICMP, as today.  Supersedes the exemption-only
routed-tso-forwarding.patch.  See CHOPPER.txt (plan) and NOTES.md
(analysis, precedents, measurements) in the if_pair repository.

Install the two new files, then apply the rest:
  cp tcp_tso.c tcp_tso.h /usr/src/sys/netinet/
  patch -p0 < software-tso-forwarding.patch   (from /usr/src)

